From: Nyxi Void packages <trophy@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shared/ad: return NULL for an absent advertising object

bt_ad_has_data returns struct bt_ad_data *, not bool. Returning false is
a type error on toolchains that distinguish _Bool from pointer types.

See also: https://github.com/bluez/bluez
--- a/src/shared/ad.c
+++ b/src/shared/ad.c
@@ -1247,8 +1247,8 @@
 struct bt_ad_data *bt_ad_has_data(struct bt_ad *ad,
 					const struct bt_ad_data *data)
 {
 	if (!ad)
-		return false;
+		return NULL;
 
 	return queue_find(ad->data, data_match, data);
 }
